BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Union Congregational Church
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260620T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260620T110000
DTSTAMP:20260618T004634
CREATED:20260610T170414Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T172201Z
UID:10004229-1781949600-1781953200@www.unioncong.org
SUMMARY:Passaic River Rally "People Over Pollution"
DESCRIPTION:Passaic River Rally “People Over Pollution” \nNewark Riverfront Park (727 Raymond Boulevard\, Newark) \nJoin Michele Sionas and others for this community-driven protest and press conference focused on environmental justice and demanding accountability for the historic pollution of the Passaic River. This event is in partnership with the Ironbound Community Corporation\, alongside a coalition of residents\, regional advocates\, and local organizations. \nThe Passaic River Rally (officially organized under the banner “People Over Pollution”) is a community-driven protest and press conference focused on environmental justice and demanding accountability for the historic pollution of the Passaic River. \nEvent Details \n• Date: Saturday\, June 20\, 2026 \n• Time: 10:00 AM – 11:00 AM \n• Location: Newark Riverfront Park (727 Raymond Blvd\, Newark\, NJ 07105) \n  \nWhat the Rally is About: \nThe demonstration is a response to decades of corporate pollution that has plagued the Passaic River—most notably the heavy dioxin contamination left behind by chemical companies like OxyChem (and its predecessors) during the mid-20th century. \nWhile the EPA has a federally approved cleanup plan in place for the lower 8.3 miles of the river\, local advocates argue that progress has been entirely too slow. The core pillars of the rally include: \n• Demanding Polluters Pay: Activists are demanding that the responsible corporations fully fund the multi-billion-dollar cleanup rather than pushing the burden onto taxpayers or attempting to legally evade liability. \n• Urgent Federal Action: Organizers are calling on federal regulators to accelerate the timeline of the actual removal of toxic sediment from the riverbed. \n• Community Health Protection: The rally highlights how the ongoing toxic presence in the water continues to disproportionately impact the health\, recreation\, and economic well-being of residents in Newark (particularly the Ironbound community) and surrounding areas.
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/passaic-river-rally-people-over-pollution/
CATEGORIES:All Church Events,All Events,Justice & Community Engagement
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Union Congregational Church
